sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-acropora-millepora-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-acropora-millepora-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-acropora-millepora-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Acropora millepora Holocene Turing wavenumber at 385.2 µm (pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 87.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the same Schnakenberg law (a=0.12, b=0.78, D_v/D_u=15.75, D_u solved so argmax σ(k) = 2π/385.2 µm) and gauge-fixes the periodic field to dihedral 6, the copy whose 12-bin Sobel orientation is closest to the Lundgren colony photograph. Orientation KS is 0.054. The comparison figure adds the nonlinear ablation inset: std(u) grows under ρ=15.75 and decays under ρ=1 (std ratio 0.048). Nonlinear FFT wavelength is 383.6 µm against the 385.2 µm target; the diffusivity sweep has Pearson r = 0.999986 and RMSE 4.06 µm. The 12-frame 720×540 GIF scores cv_sim_similarity 85.9. Murray band center remains 319.4 µm and is not claimed as the selected mode. Age is 0 Ma; the chronoseries has no other node. Overall 87.1/100 (faithfulness 86.0, reproducibility 89.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit dff4f2b508d0d1939f865c2f90f7ffe070e890d6; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/acropora_millepora_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-acropora-millepora-turing-wavelength-s0.py at dff4f2b508d0d1939f865c2f90f7ffe070e890d6, image/png, 1107243 B, 1568×1204 px, artifact_sha256 b961f6f44ace9b7168493e6db0302d044e9ed9b1fc77bc1a476480ed6ad43dac (sha256 b961f6f44ace9b7168493e6db0302d044e9ed9b1fc77bc1a476480ed6ad43dac), spec_fingerprint 9216d34e8500759b1989295cbfdfd4547358ffe09553264c746622fde6834013. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 9216d34e8500759b1989295cbfdfd4547358ffe09553264c746622fde6834013; artifact_sha256: b961f6f44ace9b7168493e6db0302d044e9ed9b1fc77bc1a476480ed6ad43dac; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/acropora_millepora_turing_wavelength_s0/acropora_millepora_gbr_lundgren2013.jpg=94c2290198c33f39..., datasets/acropora_millepora_turing_wavelength_s0/acropora_millepora_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=cf2e62d3f7797eca..., datasets/acropora_millepora_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=15285ac3d6dead24...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-acropora-millepora-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation for a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics and Gierer & Meinhardt 1972 long-range inhibition. | Murray 1981 band-center wavenumber, reported here as a contrast, not as k_c. | Dove et al. 2001 and D'Angelo et al. 2008: Acropora host GFP-like pigment is light-regulated. | Lundgren et al. 2013 CC BY 4.0 colony photograph (SHA-256 pinned). | Wallace & Rosen 2006 Eocene Acropora, outside this one-node Holocene series.; reconstructed_in_script: D_u = 881.13 µm²/s so the fastest linear mode is 384.7 µm, FFT mode 383.6 µm. | Dihedral code 6 selected by L1 distance of 12-bin Sobel histograms. | KS = 0.054 between specimen and render orientation histograms. | Equal-diffusion ablation: σ_max = -0.038 and std ratio 0.048.; transfer_boundary: 385.2 µm (3.852e-4 m, log10 = -3.414) is the assigned tier-5 detail scale. | Computer-vision similarity is scored against a centimetre-scale colony photograph.; does_not_claim: That 385.2 µm is a published measurement of A. millepora stripe spacing. | That the spot lattice segments the colony branches in the photograph. | A predecessor or successor chronospecies. Series length is 1 at 0 Ma. | That gauge-fixing raised cv_sim_similarity. Pass 1 scored 86.1 and pass 2 scored 85.9.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [independent_assessor/model-fidelity, pressure P=0.65]: Scores are from one builder-assessor (Grok 4.7). A second provider has not scored this slot.",
            "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=1.5]: A 385 µm micrograph of A. millepora chromoprotein would replace the colony photograph as the spatial target. None is in this run; the CC BY colony image stays the fitness target and the scale mismatch stays declared." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.871"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent; pass 2)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

